FWER Method 1: Bonferroni Correction
To control the FWER at level \(\alpha\) across \(m\) tests, use the per-test threshold \(\alpha^*=\frac{\alpha}{m}.\)
Recall that \(P(A \cup B) \leq P(A) + P(B)\).


Then, the FWER would be:
\[
\begin{aligned}
\operatorname{FWER}
&= P_{H_0}(\text{at least one of the $m$ null hypotheses is rejected}) \\
&= P_{H_0}\left(
\bigcup_{j=1}^{m}
\left\{p_j \leq \frac{\alpha}{m}\right\}
\right) \\
&\leq \sum_{j=1}^{m}
P_{H_0}\left(
p_j \leq \frac{\alpha}{m}
\right) \\
&= m\left(\frac{\alpha}{m}\right) \\
&= \alpha.
\end{aligned}
\]
